In article <29E29840.8239@noiro.acs.uci.edu> tvasi@shakti.bio.uci.edu (Taha K.Vasi.) writes:
>  As the subject says, how do you get a weapon's enchantment to +8 or above.
>The Wheaton spoilers claim that there is no limit (sounds unlikely). However,
>every time I tried getting my Excaliber over +5, I have failed.

There is no limit to enchanting your weapon (well, maybe it scrolls after a
while, but no limit in practical use).  However!  If you read the spoilers
more carefully you would note where it tells you that there is an
increasingly higher chance of your weapon exploding when enchanted.  Up to
+3, it will not explode when enchanted (if you get a blessed scroll of
enchant weapon, you can get it up to +6 fairly often).  At +4, there is a
1 in 2 chance of the weapon exploding, at +5 it is 1 in 3, at +6 it is 1 in
4 and so on.  Even if you find a way to increase the +, don't get it over
about +70 (I've done this in wiz mode).  Once you get to about +120 you can
kill a minotaur with one hit, but you can't defend against a goblin (or
other small creature).  I don't know if something wraps or what.

>  Now I have a +6 Excalibur and have a blessed scroll of Enchant armor. I also
>have a normal scroll. What are my chances at succeeding? 

None.  You need a scroll of Enchant Weapon.  If you had one, you would have
a 25% chance.

